1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:03,720
Looking to get started with&nbsp;
Microsoft Word? In this tutorial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:07,640
I am going to walk you through all of&nbsp;
the basics of Microsoft Word. Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

3
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:12,920
check it out. If you do not have Microsoft&nbsp;
Word already installed on your computer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

4
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:20,840
you can download it for free at office.com&nbsp;
and create a free Microsoft 365 account.

5
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:25,480
Note that the free version is a lighter&nbsp;
version and you do need internet access&nbsp;&nbsp;

6
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:32,640
in order to use it. You can also purchase&nbsp;
the Microsoft 365 subscription plan online,&nbsp;&nbsp;

7
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:38,800
which allows you to download Word as well as&nbsp;
other Microsoft 365 products directly to your&nbsp;&nbsp;

8
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:44,880
computer. To get started once you have Word&nbsp;
on your computer, if you are using Windows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

9
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:50,600
click on the Start button and you can either&nbsp;
search for Microsoft Word in the toolbar or it&nbsp;&nbsp;

10
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:56,560
is likely already going to be pinned to your Start&nbsp;
screen. On a Mac, you can find Microsoft Word in&nbsp;&nbsp;

11
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:03,400
your Applications folder or by searching for it in&nbsp;
Spotlight. To get started, you have two options.&nbsp;&nbsp;

12
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:09,560
The first is to select New Blank Document. This&nbsp;
will give you a completely blank canvas from which&nbsp;&nbsp;

13
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:16,480
to begin. The other option is to start with a&nbsp;
template by clicking on New on the left-hand side.

14
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:21,040
Here you could browse or search for&nbsp;
various templates like flyers, letters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

15
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:27,800
and address labels. If you find a template that&nbsp;
you're interested in using, click on it and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

16
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:34,440
press Create. All of the templates that you&nbsp;
see here in Word are free for you to use. Now&nbsp;&nbsp;

17
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:40,080
let's get started by clicking on New Blank&nbsp;
Document. We'll start by touring the ribbon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

18
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:45,440
which is everything that could be found here above&nbsp;
the blank page. You'll probably spend most of your&nbsp;&nbsp;

19
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:50,800
time in Microsoft Word under the Home tab, in&nbsp;
large part because this is where you'll do all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

20
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:56,280
your text formatting. I'm going to paste something&nbsp;
that I previously wrote to show you some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

21
00:01:56,280 --> 00:02:02,280
different text options available to you. Here in&nbsp;
the Font section of your ribbon, you can bold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

22
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:09,160
italicize, and underline your text. You can also&nbsp;
change the font type altogether. And you could do&nbsp;&nbsp;

23
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:13,960
this either at the beginning of writing your blank&nbsp;
document or if you've already written something,&nbsp;&nbsp;

24
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:20,560
you can highlight the text and then adjust the&nbsp;
font. Next to the font type is the font size. Some&nbsp;&nbsp;

25
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:27,960
of the other options are to add text effects, use&nbsp;
the highlighter to mark up your page, or adjust&nbsp;&nbsp;

26
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:34,600
the font color. An often overlooked feature on&nbsp;
Microsoft Word is the strike through option.&nbsp;&nbsp;

27
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:39,840
This could be helpful if you're making lists and&nbsp;
checking them off. My favorite text formatting&nbsp;&nbsp;

28
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:47,120
tool is the paintbrush. Let's say I want to&nbsp;
adjust my text formatting here. So I'm going&nbsp;&nbsp;

29
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:53,000
to change my font type and let's go ahead and&nbsp;
bold it. If I like how this works and I want to&nbsp;&nbsp;

30
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:00,120
apply the same text formatting to other areas of&nbsp;
my document, it could be a rather manual process.&nbsp;&nbsp;

31
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:06,520
However, if you click on the paintbrush once,&nbsp;
you can then apply that same text formatting to&nbsp;&nbsp;

32
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:13,640
another area in your document. If you double click&nbsp;
on the paintbrush, it locks it, allowing you to&nbsp;&nbsp;

33
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:20,520
highlight other areas in your document and apply&nbsp;
the same text formatting. This could save you a&nbsp;&nbsp;

34
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:27,120
lot of time. You will have also noticed that when&nbsp;
I highlight text in my document, a pop-up toolbar&nbsp;&nbsp;

35
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:33,760
comes up, allowing you to use some of the most&nbsp;
commonly-accessed tools, which means less toggling&nbsp;&nbsp;

36
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:39,360
if you happen to be on something besides the home&nbsp;
tab. There's also keyboard shortcuts which could&nbsp;&nbsp;

37
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:46,280
be used for some of the most popular options.&nbsp;
For instance, ctrl plus B in order to bold&nbsp;&nbsp;

38
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:52,000
text. And while our tutorial today isn't going&nbsp;
to walk through all of the keyboard shortcuts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

39
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:57,680
if you hover over any one of these icons, Word&nbsp;
will provide you with the keyboard shortcut to&nbsp;&nbsp;

40
00:03:57,680 --> 00:04:02,640
use. Now let's take a look at the paragraph&nbsp;
section. The most common reasons you would&nbsp;&nbsp;

41
00:04:02,640 --> 00:04:08,840
come here to the paragraph area is to either add&nbsp;
bullet points to your page or adjust the alignment&nbsp;&nbsp;

42
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:15,000
of your text. Let's look at the alignment first.&nbsp;
Right now, all of my text is aligned to the left&nbsp;&nbsp;

43
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:21,120
of my page. If I wanted to align my text to&nbsp;
the right, I could do that here. Likewise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

44
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:26,800
I can align my text to be centered in the middle&nbsp;
of my document. If I want to add bullet points,&nbsp;&nbsp;

45
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:31,760
you can highlight the text that you want to be&nbsp;
in a bulleted list and then you have a handful of&nbsp;&nbsp;

46
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:37,920
options in which to choose from. You also have the&nbsp;
option to add a numerical bulleted list as well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

47
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:43,600
One of the other cool features under paragraph is&nbsp;
the multi-level list. This can be really helpful&nbsp;&nbsp;

48
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:49,240
especially in research projects or school projects&nbsp;
where you want to add additional information under&nbsp;&nbsp;

49
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:54,800
each one of your bulleted items. If you're ever&nbsp;
using Word and know what you want to do but have&nbsp;&nbsp;

50
00:04:54,800 --> 00:05:00,040
forgotten where to locate the tool in which to&nbsp;
complete your task, you could click on search&nbsp;&nbsp;

51
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:05,560
and type it in which could be very helpful when&nbsp;
you're first learning how to use Word. Let's take&nbsp;&nbsp;

52
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:12,480
a look under the magnifying glass. I want to point&nbsp;
out one helpful feature which is find and replace.&nbsp;&nbsp;

53
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:17,160
If you want to locate a word or multiple words&nbsp;
in your document and replace them with something&nbsp;&nbsp;

54
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:22,920
else, let's say you spelled somebody's name&nbsp;
incorrectly or in this case if I want to change&nbsp;&nbsp;

55
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:29,960
all of the words in my document to Microsoft&nbsp;
Word. You could do that here and either replace&nbsp;&nbsp;

56
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:37,880
some, all, or just locate those words in your&nbsp;
document. In this case, Word has gone ahead and&nbsp;&nbsp;

57
00:05:37,880 --> 00:05:44,520
made four replacements on my behalf. Next is&nbsp;
another one of my favorite tools which is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

58
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:52,400
dictate button. Once you click on this microphone,&nbsp;
Microsoft Word will write down everything that&nbsp;&nbsp;

59
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:59,640
you say, allowing you to save time by just&nbsp;
speaking to your computer instead of typing.

60
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:07,760
I've actually created a separate video that&nbsp;
you can watch here in order to see all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

61
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:14,520
different features of the dictate tool, including&nbsp;
transcription. Let's move on now to the insert tab&nbsp;&nbsp;

62
00:06:14,520 --> 00:06:19,520
which is located next to the home tab. This is&nbsp;
where you come if you want to insert something&nbsp;&nbsp;

63
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:26,200
onto your page. The first one being a table. You&nbsp;
would drag and drop your mouse to select the table&nbsp;&nbsp;

64
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:32,240
size that you need created. You'll notice that&nbsp;
once you've created a table, two new tabs will&nbsp;&nbsp;

65
00:06:32,240 --> 00:06:38,480
open up here at the top, table design and table&nbsp;
layout. I created a table earlier that I'm going&nbsp;&nbsp;

66
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:43,520
to paste into my document to show you some of the&nbsp;
editing features available. The first being adding&nbsp;&nbsp;

67
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:48,800
shading to your document. This is different than&nbsp;
adjusting the font color because you're actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

68
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:54,520
changing the color of the cells itself within&nbsp;
the table. If you want to adjust the text, you&nbsp;&nbsp;

69
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:59,600
can highlight the text that you want adjusted and&nbsp;
your pop-up toolbar of font options will appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

70
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:06,760
for you. Another feature is changing the borders.&nbsp;
This can either mean changing the border style&nbsp;&nbsp;

71
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:14,080
such as the color or the type of line used as well&nbsp;
as the weight or changing the border or removing&nbsp;&nbsp;

72
00:07:14,080 --> 00:07:21,160
it entirely. In this case, I'm going to select no&nbsp;
border. This means that my text will still stay&nbsp;&nbsp;

73
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:27,720
aligned and organized in my document, but it won't&nbsp;
look like a traditional table. Here under table&nbsp;&nbsp;

74
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:34,000
layout, you can add additional cells or remove&nbsp;
them from your table without having to create&nbsp;&nbsp;

75
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:40,240
a new one. If I need to add a project number six,&nbsp;
instead of creating a new table, I can click into&nbsp;&nbsp;

76
00:07:40,240 --> 00:07:46,240
this column and click on insert to the right&nbsp;
and this will create a new column for me. Let's&nbsp;&nbsp;

77
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:53,320
say I want to remove the entire row of completion&nbsp;
information. I can select that and then come here&nbsp;&nbsp;

78
00:07:53,320 --> 00:08:01,160
to delete and delete the entire row without having&nbsp;
to recreate my entire table. Let's exit tables and&nbsp;&nbsp;

79
00:08:01,160 --> 00:08:06,960
see some of the other things that we can insert&nbsp;
into our Word document. To add a photo or image&nbsp;&nbsp;

80
00:08:06,960 --> 00:08:13,040
to your Word document, select the pictures icon.&nbsp;
You can pull an image from your device or from&nbsp;&nbsp;

81
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:18,840
a curated library of images that Microsoft&nbsp;
Word has available for free. In this example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

82
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:24,720
I'm going to drag an image from my computer and of&nbsp;
course you can always copy and paste as well. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

83
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:31,000
will open up a new picture format tab at the top&nbsp;
of my screen where you can make various artistic&nbsp;&nbsp;

84
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:37,120
edits to your picture. One of the most helpful&nbsp;
edits that you can make is to the layout options&nbsp;&nbsp;

85
00:08:37,120 --> 00:08:43,560
or format of the picture. If I were to drag this&nbsp;
image now and try to move it around my page,&nbsp;&nbsp;

86
00:08:43,560 --> 00:08:50,920
the text is going to realign. If I want the text&nbsp;
to follow the image, I can click on this and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

87
00:08:50,920 --> 00:08:57,840
select tight text wrapping. This allows my image&nbsp;
to fit in more seamlessly with the document and I&nbsp;&nbsp;

88
00:08:57,840 --> 00:09:03,640
find it particularly helpful when you're creating&nbsp;
flyers or presentations. In addition to adding&nbsp;&nbsp;

89
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:08,840
images, this is also where you would come if&nbsp;
you want to insert shapes or lines onto your&nbsp;&nbsp;

90
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:15,240
page as well as icons. And if you can't locate&nbsp;
the icon that you're looking for, you can always&nbsp;&nbsp;

91
00:09:15,240 --> 00:09:21,320
utilize the search toolbar. This is also where&nbsp;
you would find the insert chart feature. You'll&nbsp;&nbsp;

92
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:26,560
have different options available to you on the&nbsp;
left-hand side and then you can further customize&nbsp;&nbsp;

93
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:33,680
them using the variations above. Once you open one&nbsp;
of these charts, Word will guide you as to how to&nbsp;&nbsp;

94
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:40,160
input the information needed in order to create&nbsp;
the best-looking chart. In addition to inserting&nbsp;&nbsp;

95
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:46,360
things like images, this is also where you would&nbsp;
come if you want to insert a header or a footer as&nbsp;&nbsp;

96
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:51,680
well as a page number into your document. Word&nbsp;
has various options that you can pick from in&nbsp;&nbsp;

97
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:56,160
terms of templates for your header and footer.&nbsp;
It's important to note that whatever you use as&nbsp;&nbsp;

98
00:09:56,160 --> 00:10:02,440
your header or footer will appear on each page of&nbsp;
your document. Here I'll go ahead and add my text&nbsp;&nbsp;

99
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:07,360
and you can also insert images in your header and&nbsp;
footer as well. This might also be a good place&nbsp;&nbsp;

100
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:12,640
to include a date and time and you have different&nbsp;
available formats that you can choose from. Once&nbsp;&nbsp;

101
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:18,440
you're happy with how your header or footer looks,&nbsp;
you can either select close or simply click out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

102
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:23,480
that portion of their document. If you need&nbsp;
to make edits later on, simply double click&nbsp;&nbsp;

103
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:29,160
into your header or footer. Let's go ahead now and&nbsp;
add a footer onto our page. This is a good place&nbsp;&nbsp;

104
00:10:29,160 --> 00:10:34,000
to include a page number which could be found&nbsp;
over here. You'll have different options as to&nbsp;&nbsp;

105
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:40,000
how you want the page number to appear and in this&nbsp;
case I'm going to select a bottom of the page and&nbsp;&nbsp;

106
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:45,800
align it in the middle. You can highlight this and&nbsp;
change the text and coloring as well. Now in some&nbsp;&nbsp;

107
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:52,160
cases you might not want the page number to appear&nbsp;
on the first page of your document. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

108
00:10:52,160 --> 00:10:57,960
if you have a table of contents or various&nbsp;
indexes. If that's the case, go back to page&nbsp;&nbsp;

109
00:10:57,960 --> 00:11:03,880
number and select format page numbers. Here you&nbsp;
could choose what page you actually want it to&nbsp;&nbsp;

110
00:11:03,880 --> 00:11:10,480
begin at. So, if I have a multi-page document&nbsp;
instead of the one appearing on page one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

111
00:11:10,480 --> 00:11:16,000
it would actually appear on the second page of my&nbsp;
document which I want to be called page one. You&nbsp;&nbsp;

112
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:22,320
can also change the number format up here as well&nbsp;
depending on your needs. Let's now shift gears&nbsp;&nbsp;

113
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:28,080
and head over to the layout section. This is where&nbsp;
you can make changes to the margins or orientation&nbsp;&nbsp;

114
00:11:28,080 --> 00:11:35,000
of your page. Here under margins, you'll see that&nbsp;
Microsoft defaults to normal margins. This is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

115
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:40,280
space that appears on the top left right and&nbsp;
bottom of each one of your pages. If you want&nbsp;&nbsp;

116
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:45,800
to change that, let's say make the margins more&nbsp;
narrow in order to fit more on your document, you&nbsp;&nbsp;

117
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:52,040
could select one of the presets. You can also make&nbsp;
custom margins here, which could be helpful if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

118
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:57,560
have particular guidelines that you need to follow&nbsp;
for a document or presentation. You can also make&nbsp;&nbsp;

119
00:11:57,560 --> 00:12:04,760
changes to the orientation of your page, toggling&nbsp;
between portrait or landscape mode. This is also&nbsp;&nbsp;

120
00:12:04,760 --> 00:12:10,680
where you would come if you wanted to add columns&nbsp;
to your page. For example, if I needed to create a&nbsp;&nbsp;

121
00:12:10,680 --> 00:12:17,680
document with columns here, I could select this&nbsp;
and then I would have text on my left-hand side&nbsp;&nbsp;

122
00:12:17,680 --> 00:12:23,640
but I could also click into the right hand side&nbsp;
and begin typing. One keyboard shortcut that I do&nbsp;&nbsp;

123
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:31,880
want to call out is ctrl plus z. This is the undo&nbsp;
button and can be very useful when making lots of&nbsp;&nbsp;

124
00:12:31,880 --> 00:12:38,880
changes in your document, saving you lots of time.&nbsp;
Let's now move on to references. If you're putting&nbsp;&nbsp;

125
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:45,480
together a paper or presentation for school, this&nbsp;
tab can be a time saver. Let's start by looking at&nbsp;&nbsp;

126
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:50,960
how to add a table of contents. Before inserting&nbsp;
the table of contents into your document,&nbsp;&nbsp;

127
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:56,720
if you've already written something, you'll most&nbsp;
likely want to enter a new blank page into your&nbsp;&nbsp;

128
00:12:56,720 --> 00:13:03,320
document. Go back to insert and select pages. You&nbsp;
can do this at any time and it's helpful if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

129
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:10,280
want to make changes in your document midstream.&nbsp;
Select blank page and it's automatically moved all&nbsp;&nbsp;

130
00:13:10,280 --> 00:13:16,040
of your text down, leaving you with a blank page&nbsp;
to work from. You'll have a few options for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

131
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:22,320
table of contents. The first two options are&nbsp;
automatic tables and what that means is Word&nbsp;&nbsp;

132
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:28,680
will automatically look for headers within your&nbsp;
document and then automatically create a table of&nbsp;&nbsp;

133
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:34,600
contents using those headers, although you'll&nbsp;
likely always need to make small tweaks. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

134
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:40,720
other option is to insert a manual table. This is&nbsp;
where you'll go in manually and add the different&nbsp;&nbsp;

135
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:46,520
chapters or headers in your table of contents as&nbsp;
well as the corresponding page number. If you need&nbsp;&nbsp;

136
00:13:46,520 --> 00:13:53,200
to add a citation to your document, Word makes it&nbsp;
really easy. Just put your cursor next to the area&nbsp;&nbsp;

137
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:59,200
you want to insert your citation and then click&nbsp;
add new source. First, you'll select the type&nbsp;&nbsp;

138
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:04,320
of source that you want to reference and&nbsp;
then follow the prompts to put in all of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

139
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:11,960
necessary information. Once you've entered this&nbsp;
information once, Word will automatically save it&nbsp;&nbsp;

140
00:14:11,960 --> 00:14:17,200
so you don't have to recreate each citation&nbsp;
every time you need to reference it in your&nbsp;&nbsp;

141
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:23,960
document. Once you've put all of your citations&nbsp;
in, if you then choose to add a bibliography at&nbsp;&nbsp;

142
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:29,520
some point in your document, citations you've&nbsp;
already created will automatically appear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

143
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:35,560
making this super easy. Let's take a look at the&nbsp;
review tab. This is where you'll come to track&nbsp;&nbsp;

144
00:14:35,560 --> 00:14:41,360
changes and make adjustments to your documents&nbsp;
such as spelling and grammar and other proofing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

145
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:46,640
You'll notice as you're writing your document&nbsp;
that sometimes words will be underlined in red.&nbsp;&nbsp;

146
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:52,640
This means that Word is suggesting that there's an&nbsp;
error that needs to be fixed, for instance if your&nbsp;&nbsp;

147
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:59,040
spelling is off. It's as simple as right clicking&nbsp;
and then making the adjustment based off of what&nbsp;&nbsp;

148
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:05,120
Word suggests and what makes the most sense for&nbsp;
you. You can also highlight a word and you'll get&nbsp;&nbsp;

149
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:11,480
some other options if you right click it. One&nbsp;
of those is synonyms which provides you with&nbsp;&nbsp;

150
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:18,200
suggestions for other words that you might want&nbsp;
to replace it with. Here under the proofing tab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

151
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:24,400
you can select word count and this will provide&nbsp;
you with statistics in terms of your word count,&nbsp;&nbsp;

152
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:31,000
paragraphs, lines, etc. for your entire document.&nbsp;
If you want to proofread your document by having&nbsp;&nbsp;

153
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:36,760
Microsoft read it aloud to you, place your mouse&nbsp;
before the first sentence that you want the words&nbsp;&nbsp;

154
00:15:36,760 --> 00:15:45,160
to begin and then select read aloud. The most&nbsp;
common uses of Microsoft Word include writing&nbsp;&nbsp;

155
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:50,480
and editing documents, creating, etc. If you want&nbsp;
to change either the reading speed or the voice&nbsp;&nbsp;

156
00:15:50,480 --> 00:15:56,120
selection, you can do that here under settings.&nbsp;
You can add comments to your document which can be&nbsp;&nbsp;

157
00:15:56,120 --> 00:16:01,680
especially helpful if you're sharing and editing&nbsp;
this document with others for a school project or&nbsp;&nbsp;

158
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:08,160
a work assignment. Click on the document where you&nbsp;
